139,26],[20234,37.0,1956,53,144,26],[20235,37.5,1956,54,133,26],[20236,38.4,1956,54,126,25]],"links":[["Osage County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/oklahoma/osage-county"],["ARC or PLC in Osage County","/arc-plc/oklahoma/osage-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Osage County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 16 grids March to April and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years. In 2025, June to July hit 197% of normal on the middle, while November to December fell to 41%. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 26% of normal on the middle. Grid 19632 had its driest year in 1954 at 49% of normal.</p>"}
